# Development Workflow

## Day-to-day

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # first time
npm install
npm run db:generate && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed
npm run dev            # Turbo — all apps + API
```

Root scripts: `dev`, `build`, `test`, `test:e2e`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `db:*`, `docker:*`.

## Ports

Admin `3000` · Judge `3001` · Display `3002` · Public `3003` · Marketing `3004` · API `4000` · Swagger `/api/docs`.

## Local seed (dev only — not product branding)

Sample login/slug values may appear in seed/README for local bootstrapping. Prefer generic, configurable org/competition data in new seed content; do not treat NPHA/Nepal strings as product defaults.

## Rules

- Prefer `npm run dev` from repo root over starting single workspaces unless debugging one app.
- After changing `@aero-judge/shared` / `@aero-judge/utils` schemas or exports, ensure the package rebuilds (Turbo `dev` watch or `npm run build --workspace=@aero-judge/shared`).
- Do not commit secrets; use `.env` / `.env.example` patterns.
- Before committing, typecheck every workspace whose source is in the commit. Deploy builds run `tsc -b` (apps) or `tsc` (server) and fail the push when that errors. Run `npm run typecheck --workspace=<name>` for each changed workspace and do not commit if it fails. App workspace names match `apps/*` (`@aero-judge/public-results`, `@aero-judge/admin`, `@aero-judge/judge`, `@aero-judge/display`, `@aero-judge/marketing`); the API is `@aero-judge/server`. Shared package changes (`packages/shared`, `packages/utils`, `packages/ui`) need that package’s typecheck plus the apps that import it.
- DB changes go through Prisma migrations in `database/` — never edit production data ad hoc in agent flows.
